1
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:24,537
Financiero.

2
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:52,737
All of

3
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,100
A selfless public servant,

4
00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:36,017
Vice Admiral T-Borne was beloved
by Marines and citizens alike.

5
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:38,420
His sudden death shocked the world.

6
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:43,240
The Navy announced that he died in the
line of duty, but provided no details.

7
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:45,920
Have they found a killer yet?

8
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:47,540
I'm not sure.

9
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:52,957
But we've been keeping an eye on the family,
and they seem to be living comfortably.

10
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:54,380
Of course they are.

11
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:55,600
What a mess.

12
00:01:56,200 --> 00:02:00,097
Never imagined I'd live in a world
where marines are murdered by civilians.

13
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:02,768
Pirates aren't the only
ones who want money.

14
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:06,233
This was inevitable from the
moment we received bounties.

15
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:11,780
T-Bone was killed in Papa Kingdom, where
over a thousand people starve every year.

16
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:16,777
Certainly no excuse, but poverty can
drive even the sanest men to madness.

17
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:22,120
If this was all the genius Jester's
plan, then we've underestimated him.

18
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:25,057
How can we expect our
men to risk their lives

19
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:27,787
to save citizens who
are out for their blood?

20
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:31,440
We need to destroy Cross Guild soon.

21
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,957
Morale is more essential than you'd think.

22
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:37,569
A seed of doubt can
become a deadly poison.

23
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:40,880
Oh, Hina!

24
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:43,451
Have you seen Garp today?

25
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:46,037
I've got some new crackers
I want him to try.

26
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:47,500
Yeah, about that.

27
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:49,180
He set up a while ago.

28
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:51,457
He said he was going to rescue Kobe.

29
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:53,697
I think he may have taken
some members of S .W .O .R .D.

30
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:56,545
with him, which means
Kuchiku's probably there.

31
00:02:57,580 --> 00:02:58,410
What?

32
00:02:58,493 --> 00:03:00,840
You're saying they went to Fuller land?

33
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:10,600
So you survived your long
journey across the sea? Yes, sir.

34
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:12,880
Excellent work!

35
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:16,142
The whole criminal world
is singing your praises.

36
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:19,060
Three cheers for you, our evil star!

37
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:24,160
I heard the news, sir.

38
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:26,617
That you sent the money to my family.

39
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:27,530
Thank you.

40
00:03:27,613 --> 00:03:28,800
I owe you my life.

41
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:30,136
Think nothing of it.

42
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:34,060
You single-handedly killed a
vice-admiral in cold blood.

43
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:36,342
Such plenty deserves the reward.

44
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:42,977
From what I hear, those poor Marines
still haven't gotten over it.

45
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:45,589
You'd better hope that
they don't find you.

46
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:48,120
They'll chop your pretty head off.

47
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:53,640
Oh, no, I could never go
back home to my family again.

48
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:56,620
It's better than letting
them starve to death.

49
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:58,380
Don't worry, pal.

50
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:01,940
Once you join my crew, you'll
have a whole new family.

51
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:03,400
Join your crew?

52
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:05,240
Welcome to the team, pal!

53
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:07,520
No, I could never.

54
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:09,191
You don't get it, do you?

55
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:13,020
Our chairman ain't just a
pirate, he's an emperor.

56
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:17,857
Most pirates don't even get to look at
the man, let alone sail by his side.

57
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:23,560
And yet there he is, the real
deal, the bonafide buggy! Yeah!

58
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:25,870
Bonafide!

59
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:27,960
Bonafide buggy!

60
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:29,900
I like that it's catchy.

61
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:33,680
Bonafide buggy!

62
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:35,562
Bonafide buggy!

63
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:41,117
Excuse me, Chairman Bonafide buggy!

64
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:43,080
My thighs are super shapely!

65
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:44,920
I have good news, sir!

66
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:47,302
Cross-Killed's ship is all done!

67
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,188
Don't worry about the ship.

68
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:53,753
I got a team of crews that'll
whip up a real masterpiece!

69
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:57,700
Like me! That's why!

70
00:04:58,460 --> 00:04:59,290
That's right!

71
00:04:59,373 --> 00:05:00,634
We're crazy about you!

72
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:02,057
This is the King of Ships!

73
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:03,377
Do you love it or what?

74
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:04,917
We're so good at this!

75
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,235
This is how I'm done!

76
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:12,160
Hey, let it better not be our ship.

77
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:16,620
Surely you don't expect me to sail
on that ridiculous-looking thing.

78
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:18,200
Meeting room, now.

79
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:22,980
It's not my feet!

80
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:33,884
Crossgill's public reception
has been excellent.

81
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:39,246
Now that our name's out there, the Navy
will wake up to the threat that we pose.

82
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:40,960
Please, kill me.

83
00:05:41,260 --> 00:05:42,600
I'm begging you.

84
00:05:43,020 --> 00:05:44,120
It hurts.

85
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:46,440
Our goal is to create a utopia,

86
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:51,000
a military nation that won't bow to
the government or to anyone else.

87
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:53,791
And for that, only one thing is necessary.

88
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:56,019
An overwhelming amount of strength.

89
00:05:57,200 --> 00:06:00,017
This is not the life I
envisioned for myself.

90
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:01,377
I'm in hell.

91
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:04,877
But in order to acquire the
strength we need, first we...

92
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:07,000
Need wealth, fame, and power? Huh?

93
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:09,780
Sorry, I got a bit carried away.

94
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:10,920
Shut your mouth.

95
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,380
Screw this!

96
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:16,457
If you want to shut me up that
bad, just kill me already!

97
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:18,680
But, I'll tell you one last thing!

98
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:21,680
These goals you're chasing are small-time!

99
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:24,417
How can you call yourself a
pirate thinking like that?

100
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:26,080
What's this? Desperation.

101
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:27,460
You heard right.

102
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:30,998
When he finally decided it
was time to make his move.

103
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:34,217
He and I both rode on Roger's
ship back in his prime,

104
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:38,653
but for one reason or another, we
didn't make it to Laugh Tale in the end.

105
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:42,580
When you took to the sea,
you had a dream too, right?

106
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:49,680
Honestly, when I saw how much potential
Shanks had back then, I gave up my dream.

107
00:06:49,940 --> 00:06:51,140
I let it die!

108
00:06:53,940 --> 00:06:56,480
I haven't forgotten what you said, Shanks!

109
00:06:56,860 --> 00:07:00,417
You said you'd make it to Laugh
Tale on your ship! You swore!

110
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,980
Yeah, but I changed my mind.

111
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:06,006
That's not what I want
to fight for right now.

112
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,584
I'll still be a pirate, though.

113
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:11,640
I thought you were
better than that, Shanks.

114
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:16,737
I thought you'd be the one leading the
charge for the next generation of pirates.

115
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:18,040
Come with me, Buggy.

116
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:19,470
You'll see.

117
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:22,957
You think I want to work for you
after that crap he's just told me?

118
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:24,275
You're a damn coward!

119
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:27,859
Captain Roger wanted you
to follow in his footsteps.

120
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,260
Can't you see that?

121
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:32,060
I lost my treasure map because of you!

122
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:36,597
I'm sure you want to blow that off like you
do everything else, but I'm still angry!

123
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:39,560
In fact, from now on, you're my enemy!

124
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:43,500
Now he suddenly changes his mind?

125
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:47,560
After all this time, to hell with him!

126
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:51,620
Even if I just got lucky, I
am an emperor, same as him!

127
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:55,660
I want to be king!

128
00:07:56,060 --> 00:07:57,980
The king of the pirates!

129
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:02,560
Well, Gene has power, too!

130
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:06,440
We just have to find it!

131
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,540
Roger's treasure is waiting for us!

132
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:15,460
That's enough out of you!

133
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:33,033
Seems your new title is giving
you delusions of grandeur.

134
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:35,297
Should we beat some more sense into you?

135
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:38,909
Did you honestly think your
insipid speech would work on us?

136
00:08:39,160 --> 00:08:41,357
Piracy is a business,
not some little game.

137
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:43,697
You think you can be king without a plan?

138
00:08:43,780 --> 00:08:46,340
Red hair, black beard, and Straw Hat.

139
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:49,148
Those are the enemies
we would have to face.

140
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,700
Yeah, but we can outsmart them!

141
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:54,220
A treasure hunt is a race, not a war!

142
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:57,560
You made fun of my speech!

143
00:08:57,980 --> 00:09:00,620
I'll show you how inspirational I can be!

144
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:04,457
Why do you think pirates
took to the sea to chase

145
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:07,364
dreams greater than they
never dared to imagine?

146
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:11,240
Listen up, men!

147
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:17,840
Don't you even think about it.

148
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,420
Come on, tell me!

149
00:09:24,820 --> 00:09:27,360
What dream drove you to the sea?

150
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:31,060
In our world, you could
die before you know it.

151
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:35,539
Aren't your souls crying out for
something that's worth fighting for?

152
00:09:45,060 --> 00:09:46,080
He's right!

153
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:47,380
I can feel it!

154
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:49,800
My lost passion is coming back to life!

155
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:53,300
Only a coward would be
satisfied for the status quo.

156
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:56,557
If you have a dream, then chase
it with all your strength!

157
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:58,000
I've got your back.

158
00:09:58,220 --> 00:09:59,632
There's no need to fear.

159
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:05,500
There's only one goal for us now.

160
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:06,960
The One Piece!

161
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:11,030
What?

162
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:13,640
The One Piece!

163
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,700
I can see the ship.

164
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,880
You okay, pal? Just breathe.

165
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,238
We're almost there.

166
00:10:25,420 --> 00:10:26,500
Keep it together.

167
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:44,980
Hey, Ahiru! Whatcha think? A good ship?

168
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:48,860
Or a bad ship? Is it a
friend? Enemy? Who? What? How?

169
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:51,041
You know, I've been faking fears.

170
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:52,613
Quiet, I need to focus.

171
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:00,240
Warp, flag, punk.

172
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:09,260
Say, would you care to make a bet?

173
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,176
On what sort of ship that is, I mean.

174
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:13,920
I wager it's an enemy.

175
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:15,320
Are you in?

176
00:11:16,860 --> 00:11:18,140
Yeah, okay.

177
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:20,630
Woosh.

178
00:11:25,860 --> 00:11:27,420
You're on, my friend.

179
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:31,180
I'll bet that's up, oh shit.

180
00:11:31,380 --> 00:11:32,674
How's a million sound?

181
00:11:33,180 --> 00:11:34,010
Wado?

182
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:35,120
A million?

183
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:49,360
Dragon! Evil!

184
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:51,780
It's Sabo!

185
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:54,720
He finally came home to us!

186
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:58,180
Hee-haw!

187
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:00,600
That's our boy!

188
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:02,605
Why, I wasn't worried one bit!

189
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:06,380
I missed him so much!

190
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:08,540
Sabo!

191
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:33,720
Samu!

192
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:48,520
Hey guys, it's been a while.

193
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:52,140
We're not the best of all!

194
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:56,120
Damn you, Geron!

195
00:12:56,300 --> 00:12:57,777
I know you cheated somehow!

196
00:12:57,860 --> 00:12:59,480
I won't give you one berry!

197
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:02,306
Sorry, pal, but I won
the bet fair and square.

198
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:04,720
What is that?

199
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:06,409
Are you using a telescope?

200
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:07,370
I don't know.

201
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:08,740
Lying fraud!

202
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:10,440
Open your mouth!

203
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:12,030
What?

204
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:16,060
Welcome back.

205
00:13:16,260 --> 00:13:18,025
I was just about to shoot you.

206
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:20,317
Well, I'm glad you didn't, Ahiru.

207
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:23,500
Were you worried about me? Maybe. Sabo!

208
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:25,700
I'm so happy you're safe!

209
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:27,440
Hey, thanks, Ushiano.

210
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:28,677
Nice to see you.

211
00:13:28,760 --> 00:13:29,940
You little scamp!

212
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:32,157
Don't you know it's rude
to keep a queen waiting?

213
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:34,620
We were all in a stew waiting for news!

214
00:13:35,060 --> 00:13:36,707
It's been quite the journey.

215
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:39,156
Well, stop teasing and spill the tea!

216
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:42,140
This ship is from Lulusia.

217
00:13:42,300 --> 00:13:44,557
The kingdom that just
vanished into thin air?

218
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:45,470
Yeah.

219
00:13:45,553 --> 00:13:46,709
I'll explain things later.

220
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:51,580
For now, we should find
them a place to rest.

221
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:54,280
Hey, Sabo!

222
00:13:57,780 --> 00:14:00,537
How dare you go radio silence on us!

223
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:02,679
I'm sorry, but I did have a choice!

224
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:06,357
I couldn't get an encrypted
transponder snail.

225
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:07,837
They were gonna tap the line.

226
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:09,897
I couldn't risk talking any longer.

227
00:14:09,980 --> 00:14:12,937
But you guys did hear me give
the indirect call signal, right?

228
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:14,020
The three knocks?

229
00:14:14,140 --> 00:14:16,375
I was out of La Lucia, perfectly safe.

230
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:17,700
All right!

231
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:24,500
But don't ever make me
worry like that again, okay?

232
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:26,600
Okay, sorry.

233
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:36,150
Samo!

234
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:39,140
You scared us half to death!

235
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:42,020
Why do you men always have to leave?

236
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:44,137
Hi, Morley.

237
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:48,240
If you ever break my heart
like that again, I'll...

238
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:50,530
I'll...

239
00:14:52,040 --> 00:14:54,500
I can't stay bad at you.

240
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:56,360
I'm so glad you're back.

241
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:59,160
Nice to see you again.

242
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:00,610
Hello.

243
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:02,080
I remember you.

244
00:15:02,300 --> 00:15:04,241
You're the chumps from the Lucia.

245
00:15:04,700 --> 00:15:06,406
I'm sorry you lost your home.

246
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:12,180
I heard you want to join the Revolutionary
Army? Yes, ma 'am! We're ready!

247
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:13,820
Not yet, you're not.

248
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:15,660
Get some rest first.

249
00:15:16,140 --> 00:15:17,493
Sort out your feelings.

250
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:25,482
I heard what happened with Kuma.

251
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:27,000
I'm sorry.

252
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:29,360
It seems we've wasted your time.

253
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:33,517
If they program Kuma to return
to Marie Joie automatically,

254
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:37,200
our efforts may have been
futile from the start. Maybe so.

255
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:39,384
I know this is hard on you two.

256
00:15:39,620 --> 00:15:41,037
More than anyone else.

257
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:46,020
Listen, getting back to business, you can't
even share your news with the captains.

258
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,960
No, it's too dangerous.

259
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:51,237
This is something I can
only share with you.

260
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:52,300
What is it?

261
00:15:52,620 --> 00:15:55,420
The truth about what
happened at Morishois.

262
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:59,557
I'm going to tell you everything
about what I saw that day.

263
00:15:59,640 --> 00:16:01,240
The day of the reverie.

264
00:16:01,860 --> 00:16:04,507
We managed to accomplish
all of our missions.

265
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:08,018
There were three general objectives.

266
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:12,760
We declared war on the Celestial
Dragons by destroying their symbol.

267
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:17,886
Then we set as many of their slaves free
as we could, including Kuma, of course.

268
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:21,296
And then, we destroyed the
food reserves in Mariejoie.

269
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:23,368
What results have you seen?

270
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:27,780
Well, we've caught the world's
attention, which was the point.

271
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:32,357
The Navy forces were busy chasing you,
so things worked out conveniently.

272
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:33,740
In short,

273
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:37,057
12 different countries revolted
against the government,

274
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:39,022
with our encouragement, that is.

275
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:43,515
It wasn't flawless, of course, but
eight of the revolts were successful.

276
00:16:44,700 --> 00:16:47,657
The newspapers called it
the Eight Nation Revolution,

277
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:53,620
though I suppose seven would be more
accurate now that the Lucia has vanished.

278
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:57,980
One detail wasn't reported.

279
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:01,017
Our forces have been
starving out the enemy.

280
00:17:01,100 --> 00:17:04,677
Seven nations have declined
to pay their heavenly tributes

281
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:07,537
and have stopped exporting
resources to the government.

282
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:12,777
Yes, not to mention we've been attacking
government shipments all over the world!

283
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:15,977
Completely cutting off
Marie Joie's supplies.

284
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:19,217
We were warned the capital
would be impenetrable

285
00:17:19,300 --> 00:17:21,437
because it's so high above sea level.

286
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:25,240
But who cares of opposition
when we've got attrition?

287
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:27,040
Let them hide!

288
00:17:27,220 --> 00:17:29,867
They won't last a week
without money or food!

289
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:35,260
I think we'll see a response soon.

290
00:17:36,040 --> 00:17:37,800
Given our enemy, yes.

291
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:41,817
The nobles are used to getting
what they want when they want it.

292
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:46,076
For those who have known nothing but
luxury, this will be pure torment.

293
00:17:47,540 --> 00:17:52,246
They're not the sort of people who will
sit back and endure an insult like this.

294
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:54,940
They're going to dispatch
the holy knights.

295
00:17:55,220 --> 00:17:57,277
That's when the real battle begins.

296
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:59,240
Sabo! No!

297
00:17:59,700 --> 00:18:00,980
Flame Emperor Boy!

298
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:04,560
You are at the top of the
government's hit list now!

299
00:18:04,940 --> 00:18:06,477
Can we please drop the nickname?

300
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:07,501
It's ridiculous.

301
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:10,897
Like it or not, it's the
name that made you an icon.

302
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:12,817
I know you didn't kill them,

303
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:18,380
but being framed for Cobra's murder has
made you a hero to rebels worldwide.

304
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:25,077
And many of those rebels hold
a common view that anyone

305
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:28,454
who was involved with the
world government must be evil.

306
00:18:28,660 --> 00:18:31,200
Of course, the truth
isn't black and white.

307
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:36,300
Even if the system is rotten, there are
good kings alongside all the tyrants.

308
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:44,680
King Cobra of Alabasta was well-liked and
had a reputation as a kind and wise ruler.

309
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:49,240
But reputations can be
deceiving sometimes.

310
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:51,180
I agree.

311
00:18:51,660 --> 00:18:53,060
Cobra was a victim.

312
00:18:53,620 --> 00:18:55,267
And his death was a tragedy.

313
00:18:56,120 --> 00:18:59,480
But if it fueled the rebellion,
then it was necessary.

314
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:02,460
You've got conviction.

315
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:06,720
In that case, tell us everything!

316
00:19:07,140 --> 00:19:08,480
I want the truth!

317
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:10,780
What happened here?

318
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:15,760
We all cried together, trying
to make sense of what we heard.

319
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:18,959
But we never lost our faith in you.

320
00:19:25,820 --> 00:19:28,500
This is a tale from over a month ago.

321
00:19:28,940 --> 00:19:31,937
Nobles from all over the
world gathered in the holy

322
00:19:32,020 --> 00:19:35,340
land of Marichois for the
council known as the Reverie.

323
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:39,200
This is an emergency!

324
00:19:39,660 --> 00:19:42,117
Intruders have infiltrated
the land of the gods!

325
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:45,177
All citizens, evacuating Median lands!

326
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:47,440
A full-blown house explorer!

327
00:19:47,940 --> 00:19:49,587
Do something, you imbeciles!

328
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:51,660
Our lives are in danger! Yeah!

329
00:19:52,020 --> 00:19:56,079
All revolutionary army captains have
been identified on the premises!

330
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:57,840
Those bastards!

331
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:01,577
Burning down our symbol is
surely a crime worthy of death,

332
00:20:01,660 --> 00:20:04,189
but burning our food
adds insult to injury.

333
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:06,897
They're jealous of us
because they're all poor!

334
00:20:06,980 --> 00:20:09,451
When we catch those rats, heads will rule!

335
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:12,500
You gods will pay dearly
for letting this happen!

336
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:15,317
Your incompetence will
be the death of you!

337
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:17,240
We will have all of your heads!

338
00:20:21,820 --> 00:20:23,620
I told you to hurry up!

339
00:20:23,740 --> 00:20:25,640
Move, you lazy mongrel!

340
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:32,420
Are you really going to
let me burn to death?

341
00:20:32,620 --> 00:20:34,220
Move faster this instant!

342
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,200
That hurts!

343
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:48,260
I can't believe you're
going to make me walk!

344
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:50,815
You're not worth the hour you breathe!

345
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:58,080
You've been terminated, filthy beast.

346
00:21:06,460 --> 00:21:07,660
My gun!

347
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:11,260
Who in blazes are you?

348
00:21:11,740 --> 00:21:13,660
That's a human life.

349
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:16,640
Does that mean nothing to you?

350
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:18,380
Karasu!

351
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:25,666
Run to the east side of town.

352
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:28,920
I will. Thank you.

353
00:21:29,240 --> 00:21:30,920
Please, hurry, St. Blooming.

354
00:21:31,100 --> 00:21:32,937
You need to evacuate immediately.

355
00:21:33,020 --> 00:21:34,314
Damn you, Cypher-Pole.

356
00:21:34,620 --> 00:21:35,820
Where were you?

357
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:38,957
Stop your dallying and
exterminate that vermin.

358
00:21:39,040 --> 00:21:39,981
A revolutionary.

359
00:21:40,660 --> 00:21:41,540
Shoot him!

360
00:21:47,820 --> 00:21:48,650
Come at him.

361
00:21:48,860 --> 00:21:49,777
Just keep firing.

362
00:21:49,860 --> 00:21:51,997
Don't stop till you're sure he's dead!

363
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:54,139
Damn it for the dead of the switch!

364
00:21:58,060 --> 00:21:59,825
Wait, everyone hold your fire!

365
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:01,529
What happened to his body?

366
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:03,391
We killed him, didn't we?

367
00:22:03,840 --> 00:22:05,252
So where the hell is he?

368
00:22:13,220 --> 00:22:14,050
Aversuch!

369
00:22:19,860 --> 00:22:20,690
No!

370
00:22:31,860 --> 00:22:33,340
Run, trash.

371
00:22:45,860 --> 00:22:47,460
Someone help me already!

372
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:52,740
Please help!

373
00:22:52,900 --> 00:22:54,260
Let us escape too!

374
00:22:54,700 --> 00:22:57,100
We'll die if we stay chained like this!

375
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:58,840
Don't leave us!

376
00:22:59,500 --> 00:23:00,700
Well, hello!

377
00:23:03,620 --> 00:23:06,540
I'll get those chains for you! Hang tight!

378
00:23:08,860 --> 00:23:09,860
What's happening?

379
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:12,180
Nobody move, okay?

380
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:13,540
Here goes!

381
00:23:14,940 --> 00:23:16,460
Laser shooter!

382
00:23:28,520 --> 00:23:29,500
Now run!

383
00:23:29,880 --> 00:23:31,704
We're to the east side of town.

384
00:23:31,820 --> 00:23:33,996
We'll get out of this place together.

385
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:38,420
Thank you so much, Willie.

386
00:23:40,160 --> 00:23:42,100
You guys can take me later.

387
00:23:42,460 --> 00:23:43,840
Just run for now.

388
00:23:48,140 --> 00:23:49,680
That's a big one, huh?

389
00:23:54,240 --> 00:23:55,100
Lindbergh!

390
00:23:55,260 --> 00:23:56,848
We've got enemies incoming!

391
00:23:58,060 --> 00:24:00,180
Hurry up and through the slays!

392
00:24:00,500 --> 00:24:01,520
No problem!

393
00:24:05,060 --> 00:24:06,940
Something is headed this way.

394
00:24:07,640 --> 00:24:08,960
Something strong.

395
00:24:14,140 --> 00:24:15,000
No!

396
00:24:17,880 --> 00:24:19,180
Oh, no!

397
00:24:23,340 --> 00:24:28,680
Oh, oh, oh, oh,

398
00:24:29,160 --> 00:24:30,480
oh!

399
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:50,360
Get back here!

400
00:24:50,580 --> 00:24:53,560
How dare you repulsive
slaves defy my orders!

401
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:05,447
What is the meaning of this?

402
00:25:05,920 --> 00:25:09,440
Pass, did I make you
trip and fall? A giant!

403
00:25:13,380 --> 00:25:15,060
I'll be taking that.

404
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:18,720
You'll never point this
nasty thing at people again.

405
00:25:19,740 --> 00:25:22,020
Yoo-hoo, boys, time to get shaken.

406
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:24,127
Go to the east side of town.

407
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:26,753
My little friends will be expecting you.

408
00:25:30,480 --> 00:25:31,310
Go!

409
00:25:31,393 --> 00:25:33,360
And be careful! Thank you!

410
00:25:38,460 --> 00:25:41,340
You revolutionaries really piss me off!

411
00:25:48,580 --> 00:25:51,417
You know what it means to
attack the Celestial Dragons.

412
00:25:51,500 --> 00:25:54,840
The punishment for your crimes is death!

413
00:26:06,100 --> 00:26:08,180
You're the temper, don't you, Tree?

414
00:26:08,640 --> 00:26:10,760
Are you all barking no bite?

415
00:26:11,080 --> 00:26:12,433
Shut your mouth, freak!

416
00:26:12,820 --> 00:26:14,702
Why are you destroying the town?

417
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:17,216
And where the hell is your commander?

418
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:20,120
Bringing in a third on our date? Really?

419
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:21,680
You pervert!

420
00:26:22,120 --> 00:26:22,980
No, hell no!

421
00:26:23,260 --> 00:26:24,837
I'm not taking that from you!

422
00:26:24,920 --> 00:26:26,567
Look at what you're wearing!

423
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:29,320
What?

424
00:26:29,620 --> 00:26:31,340
Are you checking me out?

425
00:26:32,860 --> 00:26:34,140
My goodness!

426
00:26:34,580 --> 00:26:36,420
You're really ugly, aren't you?

427
00:26:36,860 --> 00:26:40,360
If you like me that much, just say so!

428
00:26:45,640 --> 00:26:47,360
Time to die!

429
00:26:50,940 --> 00:26:51,780
You!

430
00:26:52,180 --> 00:26:53,260
Ryo Kukyu!

431
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:56,040
Now see here!

432
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:58,600
If we're hurt, I'll have your head!

433
00:26:58,860 --> 00:26:59,860
That's a promise!

434
00:27:00,100 --> 00:27:02,057
Then get your asses out of the way!

435
00:27:02,140 --> 00:27:03,260
I'm fighting here!

436
00:27:10,860 --> 00:27:11,980
Hey, Fujitora!

437
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:14,414
What the hell are you doing down there?

438
00:27:14,800 --> 00:27:17,560
Ending this, I'm calling a meteor.

439
00:27:17,740 --> 00:27:18,917
Are you out of your mind?

440
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:19,830
Stop that!

441
00:27:21,460 --> 00:27:24,357
Two admirals if this
wasn't the land of the

442
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:27,177
gods they would have
turned this place to dust.

443
00:27:27,260 --> 00:27:31,757
They're still making
quite the mess the rebels

444
00:27:31,840 --> 00:27:33,757
aren't backing down even though they're at

445
00:27:33,840 --> 00:27:36,697
a disadvantage if they
have that much confidence

446
00:27:36,780 --> 00:27:39,400
their captains must be terribly fearsome.

447
00:27:41,080 --> 00:27:42,040
Terribly! Yuyoi!

448
00:27:43,520 --> 00:27:44,350
Fine, then.

449
00:27:44,433 --> 00:27:45,997
We'll let the admirals handle things.

450
00:27:46,080 --> 00:27:47,100
Let's move out.

451
00:28:01,180 --> 00:28:03,827
Sabo, have you found
the keys to the callers?

452
00:28:04,160 --> 00:28:05,397
I know where they are, at least.

453
00:28:05,480 --> 00:28:06,892
I should have them soon.

454
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:09,750
Hey, Lindbergh!

455
00:28:09,833 --> 00:28:11,540
That's you, Sabo? What is it?

456
00:28:11,640 --> 00:28:14,360
Kuma was heading off to
Pangaea Castle. What?

457
00:28:14,780 --> 00:28:16,000
You mean on his own?

458
00:28:16,220 --> 00:28:17,279
I saw him with St.

459
00:28:17,380 --> 00:28:19,086
Rosward and his son, Charlos.

460
00:28:23,120 --> 00:28:27,177
I think they're on their way to finish what
they started in the Mingling Courtyard.

461
00:28:27,260 --> 00:28:28,090
Wait, what?

462
00:28:30,740 --> 00:28:32,505
You're going to be my new pet.

463
00:28:32,840 --> 00:28:34,057
Just wait, my dear.

464
00:28:34,140 --> 00:28:36,980
That means Princess
Shirahoshi is in danger.

465
00:28:37,140 --> 00:28:39,728
They make Kuma do their
dirty work for them.

466
00:28:40,080 --> 00:28:40,910
Don't worry.

467
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:43,160
I'm not going to let them use him.

468
00:28:43,580 --> 00:28:44,410
Hey, Morley.

469
00:28:44,493 --> 00:28:45,380
Get ready.

470
00:28:45,760 --> 00:28:46,600
Okie Dock.

471
00:28:47,300 --> 00:28:48,241
We'll save Kuma.

472
00:28:48,600 --> 00:28:50,300
No matter what the cost.

473
00:28:54,700 --> 00:28:55,800
Hold on, Dad.

474
00:29:09,600 --> 00:29:12,777
Please return to your room
will you? Leave me alone!

475
00:29:12,860 --> 00:29:16,197
If you must know, I'm
going to ask Garp for help.

476
00:29:16,280 --> 00:29:18,797
We will provide all the
protection you need.

477
00:29:18,880 --> 00:29:20,217
Oh, will you now?

478
00:29:20,300 --> 00:29:22,120
Like you did for Shura Hachi.

479
00:29:22,740 --> 00:29:24,177
You let that happen.

480
00:29:24,260 --> 00:29:25,857
That is on you.

481
00:29:25,940 --> 00:29:29,580
They'll come after her
again and you know it.

482
00:29:35,160 --> 00:29:38,537
Your Majesty, please don't push yourself.

483
00:29:38,620 --> 00:29:41,917
I finally have a chance
to meet the five elders.

484
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:44,800
It may very well be my last.

485
00:29:50,060 --> 00:29:50,890
Halt!

486
00:29:50,973 --> 00:29:54,177
Only King Cobra has permitted an
audience with the five elders.

487
00:29:54,260 --> 00:29:55,097
What?

488
00:29:55,180 --> 00:29:56,980
Step back, you two.

489
00:29:59,100 --> 00:30:03,320
I won't be long, but I imagine it
would be quite dull to wait here.

490
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:05,936
Why don't you look after Vivi for me?

491
00:30:06,320 --> 00:30:08,100
She still gets up to mischief.

492
00:30:08,660 --> 00:30:10,740
I can't help but worry about her.
